# Hosts and patterns the link checker must not treat as failures.
#
# Keep this list short and justified. An entry here is a link nobody is
# verifying, which is exactly the situation that let the docs URL 404 for
# weeks — so prefer fixing a link over adding it here.

# Badge and one-click-deploy endpoints. They rate-limit aggressive CI callers
# and return non-200s that say nothing about whether the target is healthy.
^https://img\.shields\.io/
^https://api\.securityscorecards\.dev/
^https://securityscorecards\.dev/
^https://codespaces\.new/
^https://render\.com/deploy

# Placeholder and example hosts used in configuration snippets.
^https?://(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|0\.0\.0\.0|host\.docker\.internal)
^https?://([a-z0-9-]+\.)*example\.(com|org|net)
^https?://your-
^https?://<

# Historical prototype subtree, kept for provenance only. Its links describe a
# system that no longer exists and are deliberately not maintained.
plans/cyble-aisoc/

# Vendor docs that block datacentre egress outright.
^https://www\.linkedin\.com/
^https://twitter\.com/
^https://x\.com/
